drt: filter check_drc markers by worker check region

Upstream bug: https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD/issues/11697
Upstream fix: https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD/pull/11698
(the source changes of that pull request, without its tests, rebased onto
the OpenROAD that nixpkgs pins here).

check_drc runs one checking worker per tile of 7x7 gcells, loading routed
objects within the tile grown by MTSAFEDIST. Routed vias are found by their
whole bounding box and wires by their own, so a worker at a tile edge can
load two vias of a net but not the wire joining them, and it reports a
spacing violation between the via pads that the full design does not have.
getDRCMarkers kept every worker's markers inside the requested box; this
keeps only those inside the worker's own check region, as routing workers
already do. See docs/openroad-check-drc-tiling.md for how it was found.

diff -ru a/src/drt/src/gc/FlexGC.cpp b/src/drt/src/gc/FlexGC.cpp
--- a/src/drt/src/gc/FlexGC.cpp
+++ b/src/drt/src/gc/FlexGC.cpp
@@ -206,6 +206,11 @@
   impl_->drcBox_ = in;
 }
 
+const odb::Rect& FlexGCWorker::getDrcBox() const
+{
+  return impl_->drcBox_;
+}
+
 const std::vector<std::unique_ptr<frMarker>>& FlexGCWorker::getMarkers() const
 {
   return impl_->markers_;
